---
/** A full-width band with a mono section label down the left. */
interface Props {
  label: string;
}

const { label } = Astro.props;
---

{/*
 * `md:mt-1` puts the label's caps on the same line as the first line of the
 * text beside it. Both boxes already start at the top of the row, but the type
 * inside them does not: the label is 13px with the browser's own leading, while
 * body copy is 17px at 1.6, and that leading is split above and below every
 * line. So the prose starts about 4px lower than the label does, and the row
 * reads as though the heading has floated up.
 *
 * Only from md, because below it the grid is one column and the label sits on
 * its own line, where there is nothing to align it to.
 */}
{/*
 * The label overrides `mono-label`'s grey to the top of the ramp, and that is a
 * hierarchy fix rather than a decorative one. Every band's prose is
 * `text-ink-muted`, which is the colour `mono-label` already carries: at `md`
 * the grid holds them apart and identical greys read as one system, but below
 * it the heading sits directly on top of its paragraph in the same grey at a
 * smaller size, which is a caption above prose rather than a title over it.
 * `ink` against `ink-muted` is the step that was missing. It applies at both
 * widths, since the desktop pairing was quiet rather than wrong.
 *
 * The size goes with it, 0.75rem to 0.8125rem. That is the top of the range
 * structural type already runs in rather than a new size, so the band heading
 * is now the largest of the mono labels instead of the same as the smallest.
 * Colour alone left it reading as a bright caption; a step of size is what
 * makes it read as a heading.
 *
 * Only the band heading moves. The other `mono-label` users caption a value
 * rather than head a section: the figures band's `ARTISTS` is meant to sit
 * under its own 100px number, not compete with it.
 */}
<div class="border-hairline grid gap-6 border-t py-14 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
  <h2 class="mono-label text-ink text-[0.8125rem] md:mt-1">{label}</h2>
  <div><slot /></div>
</div>
